    "created_at": "2021-04-09T17:19:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-04-09T17:19:15Z",
    "body": "I personally think the way things work today makes a great deal of sense. All URLs are resolved relative to the base element. It doesn't matter what character they start with; they all go through the spec equivalent of `new URL(urlString, baseURL)`. Creating a less-uniform behavior would be bad IMO.",
